From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: a hosting program gets its runtime-loaded callback once, and its default domain binds by its configuration

A native program that hosts the runtime (Visual Studio's devenv.exe):
- The ICLRMetaHost::RequestRuntimeLoadedNotification callback ran before the
  runtime was loaded, on every load attempt. A callback that calls back into
  the runtime (after its thread-set call, as documented) started the load
  again and was called again, until the stack overflowed. It now runs once,
  after the runtime is loaded, and a GetInterface from it finds that runtime.
- The default domain did not bind with the program's configuration. Only a
  managed program's <probing privatePath> was used, and <codeBase> not at all.
  The privatePath of the configuration now applies to the default domain of
  any program, and <dependentAssembly> <bindingRedirect>/<codeBase> entries
  are used before probing, as the CLR does.
---
